From: Lars <118484383+LarzVader@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sysfb: simpledrm: report the connector as DSI

On the Jeazans C107 tablet simpledrm takes over the picture on the built-in
MIPI-DSI panel that the vendor U-Boot has set up, there is no other display.
The connector type Unknown makes KWin treat it as an external screen: it only
rotates outputs automatically if they are internal (LVDS, eDP or DSI), so the
orientation sensor has no effect.

Local to this tablet, not meant for upstream, where simpledrm cannot know what
kind of display it is driving.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c
@@ -840,7 +840,7 @@
 
 	connector = &sdev->connector;
 	ret = drm_connector_init(dev, connector, &simpledrm_connector_funcs,
-				 DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_Unknown);
+				 DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DSI);
 	if (ret)
 		return ERR_PTR(ret);
 	drm_connector_helper_add(connector, &simpledrm_connector_helper_funcs);
